@startuml
actor PE
participant Console
participant "Scoped monitoring service" as Service
participant "Owned target / binding repository" as Repository
participant "Scoped resource detail" as Resources
participant "Credential-backed Kubernetes verifier" as Kubernetes
participant "Private credentials resolver" as Secrets
participant "Prometheus / Loki adapters" as Adapter
participant "Prometheus / Loki" as Sources
participant "Preview / operation admission" as Admission
participant "Git/Fleet delivery" as CD
participant Alertmanager
participant "Test receiver" as Receiver
PE -> Console : Register/test connection; bind signals and profiles
Console -> Service : Authorized request with expected revision
Service -> Repository : Validate organization, generation, cluster and CAS
opt Resource observations declared
 Service -> Resources : Verify scoped resource ID and generation
 Service -> Service : Validate keys against effective collector profile
end
Service -> Secrets : Resolve each source credential privately
Service -> Adapter : Test connectivity, identity and coverage
Adapter -> Sources : Bounded read
PE -> Console : Preview monitoring/workload changes
Console -> Admission : Snapshot desired config and monitoring pins
Admission --> Console : Pending UPDATE and pinned Preview token
PE -> Console : Deploy reviewed changes
Console -> Admission : Claim Environment with current revisions
Admission -> CD : Workload + owned PodMonitor / PrometheusRule
CD -> Sources : Operator/discovery consumes desired config
CD -> Repository : Persist acknowledged monitoring signature
Console -> Service : Read app/Environment/time
Service -> Repository : Authorize; restore owned physical targets
opt Resource detail read
 Service -> Resources : Authorize resource before provider read
end
Service -> Adapter : Server-built scoped metric/log queries
Adapter -> Sources : Bounded read; no raw client selector
Sources --> Service : Samples, timestamps, gaps, logs, alerts
Service -> Repository : Read acknowledged monitoring revision
Service -> Kubernetes : Verify physical target and owned live artifact specs
Service --> Console : Config status, data coverage and mapped observations
Sources -> Alertmanager : Prometheus firing / resolved
Alertmanager -> Receiver : Grouped/inhibited actual test notifications
PE -> Console : Select native signals; Preview/Deploy withdrawal
Console -> Admission : Revision-fenced cleanup deployment
Admission -> CD : Withdraw only app-owned monitoring objects
Console -> Service : Unbind with expected revision
Service -> Kubernetes : Verify owned monitoring config absent
Service -> Repository : Remove binding with generation/CAS guards
note over Repository, Sources : Shared stack and retained history remain
note over Console, Receiver : Processing state is not delivery proof; absent data is not recovery
@enduml
